# Secrets — NEVER commit these.
# `.env.example` is the tracked template and must survive the wildcard below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Local artifacts
*.log
preview_*.png
st*.log
.DS_Store

# Design scratch — the SOURCE of the identity, not the identity itself.
# logos/*.svg and logos/LOGOS.md ARE tracked: they are the shipped assets and
# their contract. What is excluded is the exploration that produced them —
# candidate boards, a Gemini render, a zip of options. Roughly 900KB of dead
# weight in a repo that is cloned on every Community Cloud deploy, and none of
# it is reachable from the running app.
assets/candidates/
docs/brand/
*.zip

# Agent / design-tool working state.
#
# The line here is SHARED config in, PERSONAL state out. `.claude/agents/*.md`
# and `CLAUDE.md` are tracked on purpose: they are checked-in project
# configuration, the same category as `.editorconfig`, and a collaborator wants
# them. What follows is one machine's scratch — session caches, superseded
# critiques, and the design specs of build sessions that have already landed in
# CLAUDE.md. Ignored in the repo rather than only in a personal global ignore,
# so a fresh clone behaves the same for everyone.
.claude/settings.local.json
.impeccable/
.impeccable-critique-shots/
docs/superpowers/
